RCP/M DISK IMAGE FORMATS AND HOST MAINTENANCE

These are z80pack cpmsim RAW sector images: no DSK/IMD container header,
partition table or embedded geometry. The .dsk suffix does not identify a
format. Each drive has a fixed geometry in this cpmsim build; renaming an
arbitrary CP/M image to drivea.dsk or GAME.dsk does not convert it.

The bundled runtime/diskdefs is the cpmtools format reference used to build
and maintain these images. Keep it with the matching host tools.

Drive    cpmtools format    Tracks  Sectors/track  Bytes/sector  Exact bytes
A:       ibm-3740              77       26             128          256256
I:, J:   z80pack-hd           255      128             128         4177920
P:       z80pack-hdb          256    16384             128       536870912

A: is 250.25 KiB total; I:/J: are 4080 KiB (nominal 4 MB); P: is 512 MiB.
These are total image sizes, not free file-storage capacity.

Format        Block bytes  Directory entries  Reserved boot tracks  Skew
ibm-3740          1024             64                   2               6
z80pack-hd        2048           1024                   0               0
z80pack-hdb      16384           8192                   0               0

The hard-disk images have their directory at byte zero: 32768 bytes on I:/J:,
262144 bytes on P:. A: has reserved system tracks AND a skewed sector layout;
use a format-aware tool, not a guessed contiguous directory offset.

The diskdefs entries say 'os 2.2' for the on-disk directory conventions. The
guest operating system is banked CP/M 3; that setting does not select CP/M 2.2
or replace the configured sector geometry.

1. BEFORE HOST EDITING

Stop the emulator cleanly with SYSUTLS:BYEBYE and copy the image as a backup.
Do not edit a disk still open in cpmsim, even if no caller is connected.
Do not use host edits to bypass caller permissions while a guest is running.

From the unpacked package directory in a Mac/Linux shell, configure the
bundled cpmtools definitions:

    export DISKDEFS="$PWD/runtime/diskdefs"

The native launcher sets this for its own tools automatically. When calling
tools manually, set it yourself. These bundled cpmtools use direct POSIX I/O;
no libdsk installation or driver selection is required. Earlier libdsk-backed
builds misread one of this project's guest-written I: files; use these tools
and the specified geometry rather than mixing cpmtools builds/settings.

Names in host cpmtools commands use a numeric USER prefix such as 0: or 13:.
They do not resolve Z-System directory aliases like SYSUTLS: or SIGM:.
Quote wildcard specifications so the HOST shell does not expand them.
CP/M names use 8.3 characters, and user areas range from 0 through 15 here.

2. LIST, EXTRACT, ADD AND DELETE FILES

List public system files and private system tools while the guest is stopped:

    ./runtime/cpmls -f ibm-3740 disks/drivea.dsk '0:*'
    ./runtime/cpmls -f z80pack-hd disks/drivei.dsk '13:*'
    ./runtime/cpmls -f z80pack-hdb disks/drivep.dsk '0:*'

Extract the welcome banner or a library to a host file:

    ./runtime/cpmcp -f ibm-3740 disks/drivea.dsk 0:WELCOME.TXT welcome.txt
    ./runtime/cpmcp -f z80pack-hdb disks/drivep.dsk 1:CPMUG001.LBR CPMUG001.LBR

Replace a file by removing its old entry and importing its replacement:

    ./runtime/cpmrm -f ibm-3740 disks/drivea.dsk 0:WELCOME.TXT
    ./runtime/cpmcp -f ibm-3740 disks/drivea.dsk welcome.txt 0:WELCOME.TXT

Use CRLF line endings for guest text. Binary copies preserve raw bytes;
CP/M files have record-sized storage and extracted files may include trailing
record padding. Do not apply text conversion to programs or LBR archives.
The cpmcp -t option is available for intentional host/CP/M text conversion.

SYS attributes are stored on disk but do not enforce permissions. To set or
clear SYS, for example on the private PATH command:

    ./runtime/cpmchattr -f ibm-3740 disks/drivea.dsk s 0:PATH.COM
    ./runtime/cpmchattr -f ibm-3740 disks/drivea.dsk ms 0:PATH.COM

's' adds SYS; 'm' reverses following flags, so 'ms' removes SYS while retaining
other attributes. 'r' adds read-only; 'mr' removes read-only. These affect
CP/M directory attributes, separately from host filesystem permissions and
the BYE caller-access checks. Keep the release's documented A0 policy when
finishing maintenance.

3. CREATE A NEW SWAPPABLE J: IMAGE

Use a NEW name, 1-8 letters/digits/underscores, with the .dsk extension.
MOUNT recognizes these files under volumes/. All such catalog volumes are
caller-readable when mounted. Keep private sysop media under offline/, not
in volumes/. Do not leave private media mounted when returning to callers.

Example creating a blank 4177920-byte image on macOS or Linux:

    (
    set -e
    test ! -e volumes/NEW.dsk
    dd if=/dev/zero of=volumes/NEW.dsk bs=16384 count=0 seek=255
    ./runtime/mkfs.cpm -f z80pack-hd volumes/NEW.dsk
    ./runtime/cpmcp -f z80pack-hd volumes/NEW.dsk README.TXT 0:README.TXT
    ./runtime/cpmls -f z80pack-hd volumes/NEW.dsk '0:*'
    chmod 444 volumes/NEW.dsk
    )

Run these steps only after the test confirms NEW.dsk does not exist. The
parenthesized command group stops if the existence check fails.
The dd step sets the exact full length; mkfs.cpm alone may only write the
directory/reserved regions. An undersized image will fail MOUNT's geometry
validation. Never format an existing image you intend to keep.

Start RCP/M, then type MOUNT /L and MOUNT NEW. The image is opened read-only
for callers. To modify it later, stop RCP/M, 'chmod u+w volumes/NEW.dsk', make
your changes with cpmtools and restore 'chmod 444' before starting again.

For a host image editor on Windows, use a raw CP/M image editor configured
with the exact geometry above, or a compatible cpmtools build plus the same
diskdefs. A program offering a generic '.dsk' format may mean a different
container. This first release includes only macOS ARM64 host executables;
the table describes platform-independent disk bytes.

4. CREATING OTHER DISK TYPES

An I:-style blank image uses the same steps as J:. It does not create the
release's SYSUTLS contents or RBBS data files automatically.

A NEW empty P:-style archive is exactly 536870912 bytes:

    (
    set -e
    test ! -e EMPTY-P.dsk
    dd if=/dev/zero of=EMPTY-P.dsk bs=16384 count=0 seek=32768
    ./runtime/mkfs.cpm -f z80pack-hdb EMPTY-P.dsk
    )

This creates an EMPTY archive, not SIGM/CPMUG. Preserve the supplied P: or
rebuild collections with the supplied source/rcpm/build_archive.py instructions.
The distributed ARCHIVE.sha256 records all 403 original library checksums.

Formatting a blank 256256-byte ibm-3740 image does NOT make a bootable A:.
The system tracks, loader, CP/M 3 BIOS/BDOS and startup files must agree.
For normal maintenance, clone the supplied A: and change selected files
using cpmtools. Full boot-media generation is documented in the included
source/building material; do not copy boot tracks between unrelated formats.

5. HOST PROTECTION VERSUS CP/M PROTECTION

A: and I: are writable host files so the sysop and board can maintain them.
BYE restricts caller mutations and program loads inside the guest. Programs
copied to WORK do not become executable. P: and swappable J: archive images
are also host read-only. Removing a SYS attribute does not grant execution
or directory access. Do not remove the release guards to run an unreviewed
compiler, interpreter or game in a caller session.

5. SWAPPABLE P: ARCHIVES AND DIRECTORY MARKERS

Place raw z80pack-hdb images of exactly 536870912 bytes in archives/NAME.dsk.
Keep the existing 4177920-byte J: images under volumes/. MOUNT rejects images
with the wrong size for the selected drive, even if they are in the right
folder. A raw image has no geometry header: matching size is necessary, not
proof of a correctly prepared filesystem.

MOUNT P: /L lists compatible archive images. MOUNT P: NAME swaps P:.
MOUNT P: /DEFAULT restores disks/drivep.dsk. J: remains independently mounted.
Default mounts return when the emulator process restarts, not at each logoff.

NDSCAN refreshes the selected drive's names after a successful swap. To name
a user area, create an extensionless -NAME file there (up to 7 uppercase
letters/digits/underscores after the hyphen). Marker contents are irrelevant.
Create these files with CP/M or matching cpmtools while the image is unmounted.
Names are not AUTH grants. Run NDSCAN P: independently after marker changes.
Copy archives/ in backups and keep private media outside public catalogs.
